414:
(a) Any person, firm, or corporation desiring to operate a gasoline station, travel center, or other fueling center or any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail in the City of Byron shall submit an application for a license to the city administrator or his/her designee prior to seeking any other permit for land disturbance, building or other construction.
(b) In addition to any other requirements under this Code, local, state, or federal law, requirements, rules or regulations, the application shall include, but not be limited to, the following information:
(1) Name, age, and residence address of the owner-applicant;
(2) If the owner-applicant is a corporate entity, the names and addresses of the officers or members, the name and address of the registered agent, the state, county, and date of incorporation or formation, and the complete names and addresses of the administrator or administrators of the proposed gasoline stations, travel centers, other fueling centers, and any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail;
(3) The address of the location where the gasoline stations, travel centers, other fueling centers, and any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail, is to be located and operated;
(4) Any previous experience the administrator and owner(s) have had in the operation of gasoline stations, travel centers, other fueling centers, and any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail, or similar businesses;
(5) Any gasoline stations, travel centers, other fueling centers, and any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail license history of the owner-applicant and the administrator, including whether such person in any previous operation in any jurisdiction has had such a license revoked or suspended, the reason therefor, and any business activity or occupation subsequent to the action of suspension or revocation;
(6) The name and address of the owner of the property where the gasoline stations, travel centers, other fueling centers, and any establishment where gasoline or other motor vehicle fuel is sold at retail is to be located; and
(7) A complete set of fingerprints of the applicant(s), the administrator(s), and the owner(s), if alcohol of any kind is sold.
